Scientific reasoning and method (@scientific-reasoning-and-method: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_1M32MPPA03R1H4RJ3M3SSG8TXT
Scientific reasoning connects questions, observations, models, predictions, and evidence. The material examines how explanations are proposed, tested, criticised, and revised, including causality, uncertainty, competing hypotheses, and the difference between a useful model and the world it describes.

**Common preparation developed:** [Intervention questions](../../core/Define-the-intervention-and-the-outcome-before-interpreting-a-comparison.lingua) begin the eighth inquiry block. Explicit identification assumptions, competing causal accounts with the same observed law, adjustment/selection counterexamples and sensitivity reasoning prepare branch entry. Full scientific-method, advanced causal and independent research formation remain pending.

**Parent:** [Reasoning and communication](../Reasoning-and-communication.lingua#r_4HHN23A6WFE0YZ8394FZ4A5DTB).
} r_1M32MPPA03R1H4RJ3M3SSG8TXT
